          question: "What do you check and what do you change?",
          discussion: "First check your insurance terms for pregnancy and confirm she has no complications her midwife has flagged. At fourteen weeks she is past the first trimester, so many therapists would treat with adaptations, but your policy decides. Leave out the essential oil blend and use an unfragranced oil, because rosemary in particular is one many references advise avoiding in pregnancy and her nausea may make scent unpleasant anyway. Raise the head of the bed and support her with cushions, keep spells with her head back short, offer water, keep heat moderate, and bring her up slowly. Update her record to note the pregnancy and the changes, and ask her to tell you of any change at each visit.",
